<title>CHINA: China Jan-Feb sugar imports slump 35.8 percent.</title>
<headline>China Jan-Feb sugar imports slump 35.8 percent.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>China imported 40,000 tonnes of sugar in January and February, down by 35.8 percent from the year-ago period, customs figures showed on Tuesday.</p>
<p>China imported 30,000 tonnes of sugar in February alone, the figures showed.</p>
<p>Sugar exports were 20,620 tonnes in January and February, down by 88.0 percent from the same period of 1996, the figures showed.</p>
<p>Exports reached 14,855 tonnes in February, the figures showed.</p>
<p>-- Beijing newsroom (8610) 6532-1921</p>
